{"author":{"id":"1d5f412cdeafe9987ad9876b0995bf5032718543d34c038a50cdb41808e9874c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788305127,"nonce":"2nhNyAho82KeyuQult7GuM9Q0lQ=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOULVc1M8AAAABPPhgHg","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/torram-ng/issues/10","origin":"github"},"title":"suggest_method can return the string 'None', causing an infinite loop under -ss","message":"`suggest_method()` initialises `fullest_file_idx = None` and returns `str(fullest_file_idx)` at the end. When `file_infos` is empty — which happens if every candidate was filtered out as a hardlink — the loop never runs and the function returns the literal string `\"None\"`.\n\nBack in `guess_file()`:\n\n```python\nwhile True:\n    user_input = \"\"\n    if args.autoskip \u003c 2 and not (suggestion == \"S\" and args.autoskip \u003e 0):\n        user_input = input(...)\n    if user_input == \"\":\n        user_input = suggestion\n    if re.match(\"^[0-9]+$\", user_input): ...\n    elif user_input.upper() == \"M\": ...\n    elif user_input.upper() == \"S\": ...\n    elif user_input.upper() == \"A\": ...\n    else:\n        print(\"Mmmm?\")\n```\n\nWith `-ss` (`autoskip == 2`) no input is read, `user_input` becomes `\"None\"`, no branch matches, and the loop prints `Mmmm?` forever with no way to make progress.","files":null}]}